{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.MathlibExt.QuantumDilogarithm","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.QuantumDilogarithm","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.BigOperators.Group.Finset.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic"],"declarations":8,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.QuantumDilogarithm.qPochProd_q_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.QuantumDilogarithm.qPochProd_q_zero","kind":"theorem","line":96,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/QuantumDilogarithm.lean#L96-L104","doc":"At `q = 0` every factor collapses to `1` — since `2n+1 ≥ 1` we have\n`0 ^ (2n+1) = 0`, so `1 + 0 ^ (2n+1) * x = 1` for *every* `n` (the first\nfactor included) — hence $P_N(0, x) = 1$ for all `N` (the classical,\nundeformed truncation is trivial). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.QuantumDilogarithm.qPochProd_zero_arg","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.QuantumDilogarithm.qPochProd_zero_arg","kind":"theorem","line":90,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/QuantumDilogarithm.lean#L90-L94","doc":"The constant term is `1`: $P_N(q, 0) = 1$ for every `N`\n(the formal-power-series normalisation $\\Phi_q(0) = 1$). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.QuantumDilogarithm.qPochProd_functional","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.QuantumDilogarithm.qPochProd_functional","kind":"theorem","line":82,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/QuantumDilogarithm.lean#L82-L88","doc":"**Functional equation** (discrete `q`-difference precursor of $\\Phi_q$),\nthe `M = 1` case of [`qPochProd_add`](#QOU.MathlibExt.QuantumDilogarithm.qPochProd_add):\n$$P_{N+1}(q, x) \\;=\\; (1 + q x)\\,P_N(q,\\; q^2 x),$$\nthe finite shadow of $\\Phi_q(q^2 x) = (1 + q x)\\,\\Phi_q(x)$. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.QuantumDilogarithm.qPochProd_add","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.QuantumDilogarithm.qPochProd_add","kind":"theorem","line":68,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/QuantumDilogarithm.lean#L68-L80","doc":"**Index additivity (cocycle identity).** Splitting the product after the\nfirst `M` factors and re-indexing the tail rescales the argument by `q^{2M}`:\n$$P_{M+N}(q, x) \\;=\\; P_M(q, x)\\,\\cdot\\,P_N(q,\\; q^{2M} x).$$\nThis is the finite backbone from which both the functional equation\n(`M = 1`, below) and — in the limit — the multiplicative cocycle of\n$\\Phi_q$ under the `q`-shift descend. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.QuantumDilogarithm.qPochProd_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.QuantumDilogarithm.qPochProd_one","kind":"theorem","line":64,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/QuantumDilogarithm.lean#L64-L66","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.QuantumDilogarithm.qPochProd_succ","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.QuantumDilogarithm.qPochProd_succ","kind":"theorem","line":59,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/QuantumDilogarithm.lean#L59-L62","doc":"Peel the **last** factor: $P_{N+1} = P_N \\cdot (1 + q^{2N+1} x)$. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.QuantumDilogarithm.qPochProd_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.QuantumDilogarithm.qPochProd_zero","kind":"theorem","line":55,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/QuantumDilogarithm.lean#L55-L57","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.QuantumDilogarithm.qPochProd","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.QuantumDilogarithm.qPochProd","kind":"def","line":48,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/QuantumDilogarithm.lean#L48-L53","doc":"Finite `q`-Pochhammer denominator product\n$P_N(q, x) = \\prod_{n=0}^{N-1} (1 + q^{2n+1} x)$, i.e. the truncation\n$(-qx; q^2)_N$ whose reciprocal limit is the compact quantum dilogarithm\n$\\Phi_q(x)$. ","signatureChunk":0}]}